```java
clientParams = new ModifiableSolrParams();
client = HttpClientUtil.createClient(clientParams, clientConnectionManager);
```
Reason:
The `UpdateShardHandler` initializes the `clientParams` without setting the connection and read timeout configurations, which results in these timeouts being ignored when creating the HTTP client. The configuration settings for these timeouts were not appropriately accounted for after the changes made in SOLR-4509.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```java
clientParams.set(HttpClientUtil.PROP_SO_TIMEOUT, cfg.getDistributedSocketTimeout());
clientParams.set(HttpClientUtil.PROP_CONNECTION_TIMEOUT, cfg.getDistributedConnectionTimeout());
```
Reason:
These statements update the `clientParams` with the appropriate timeout values from the configuration (`cfg`), ensuring that the connection and read timeouts are correctly applied when creating the HTTP client. This modification rectifies the oversight from SOLR-4509 and allows the timeouts to be set as intended.


